WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.103
Passive network telemetry often gives hunters broad visibility without actively querying sensitive devices.

00:00:07.103 --> 00:00:13.715
It can show assets, peers, protocols, timing, and communication across trust boundaries.

00:00:13.715 --> 00:00:20.328
Protocol-aware sources may add sessions, reads, writes, commands, errors, or engineering operations.

00:00:20.328 --> 00:00:29.390
Firewall, VPN, jump-host, and vendor-access logs describe boundary connections, identities, source systems, approvals, destinations, and session duration.

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:38.942
HMI and engineering-workstation records may add logons, processes, project access, file activity, removable media, and connections to controllers.

00:00:38.942 --> 00:00:43.595
Historian data connects cyber observations to physical behavior.

00:00:43.595 --> 00:00:52.657
Trends, alarms, setpoints, and equipment state can show whether a technical event coincided with an operational change.

00:00:52.657 --> 00:00:59.270
Authentication events add account lifecycle, failed access, privilege, and unusual user timing.

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:08.821
Controller change records, project repositories, and management tools may report downloads, mode changes, firmware work, or configuration differences.

00:01:08.821 --> 00:01:17.883
These records are valuable when network traffic is encrypted or when the hunt concerns local engineering activity.

00:01:17.883 --> 00:01:21.067
Every source has blind spots.

00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:28.659
Passive sensors miss unobserved segments, serial devices behind gateways, dormant assets, and local actions.

00:01:28.659 --> 00:01:31.843
Endpoint logging may be incomplete.

00:01:31.843 --> 00:01:37.476
Historians may show an effect without identifying who initiated it.

00:01:37.476 --> 00:01:42.130
Inconsistent clocks or asset names make correlation unreliable.

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:48.743
Before hunting, document coverage, time synchronization, retention, field quality, and source ownership.

00:01:48.743 --> 00:01:52.906
Protect sensitive telemetry and preserve original evidence.

00:01:52.906 --> 00:02:03.927
A strong hunt combines complementary sources, states what the data can and cannot prove, and adjusts confidence when visibility is incomplete.
